## Decision

**action: `no_action`**

I found strong, directly-applicable evidence in this repo rather than needing to speculate: Spring Boot 4.x renamed many "starter" modules by dropping the `-starter-` infix (confirmed by `spring-boot-testcontainers`, `spring-boot-h2console`, `spring-boot-jdbc`, etc. already present in `metadata/org.springframework.boot/`). `spring-boot-data-couchbase-test` is this renaming applied to `spring-boot-starter-data-couchbase-test`.

Two pieces of existing metadata make the call for me:
- `metadata/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-starter-data-couchbase-test/index.json` — already marked `not-for-native-image: true`: *"Artifact JAR contains no JVM class files, so there is no library code for native-image metadata."*
- `metadata/org.springframework.boot/spring-boot-starter-couchbase-test/index.json` — the sibling non-`data` variant, **at the exact same version 4.1.1** as this issue — marked `not-for-native-image: true`: *"The published spring-boot-starter-couchbase-test-4.1.1 JAR contains only META-INF/MANIFEST.MF, LICENSE.txt, and NOTICE.txt, with no JVM class files; it is a dependency starter whose runtime classes are supplied by its dependencies."*

These Spring Boot `*-test` starters are deliberately empty POM-style aggregators — their only purpose is to pull in `spring-boot-test`, `spring-boot-couchbase`, `spring-boot-testcontainers`, and `org.testcontainers:couchbase` transitively for users' own test classpaths. There's no library code in the artifact itself to drive coverage into, so no Docker image, extra Maven dependency, or environment/system-property setup can make "meaningful coverage" reachable — there's nothing to reach. The standard scaffold already has the right idiom for this (the `not-for-native-image` empty-JAR path used for the four sibling Couchbase-test artifacts), and that's what should apply here too, pending the authoritative local Gradle/Native Image check.

